# Phase 20 canonical URL contract (docs/baseline/2026-09-07-phase20/CANONICAL_URL_CONTRACT.md):
# trailing slash is canonical for every indexable page. Cloudflare's static-assets
# binding already redirects these bare paths to their trailing-slash form by
# default (`html_handling: auto-trailing-slash`), but as a 307 Temporary Redirect —
# confirmed live in production, 2026-09-07 — which Google treats differently from a
# permanent move. These explicit rules force a 301 instead, one hop, for exactly the
# prerendered routes listed in `apps/web/src/lib/route-registry.ts`'s
# `PRERENDERED_ROUTES` (kept in sync by `route-registry.test.ts`). SSR pages have no
# static asset and are handled separately in `middleware.ts`.
#
# Exact-match rules first, wildcard/placeholder rules last — `wrangler` warns that
# placing a splat/placeholder rule above an exact one makes matching less efficient.
/about /about/ 301
/contact /contact/ 301
/audit /audit/ 301
